Phase 8 M8.9 (sandbox-loss recovery, E2E-018) — loss detection + reconciliation proof
Date: 2026-09-13

REAL PROCESSES: the guest agent is HARD-KILLED mid-operation (the
substrate loss event). The blocked in-flight caller gets a classified
loss (outcome UNKNOWN — dropped connection or expired bounded wait;
typed guest refusals are known outcomes, never 'lost'). A FRESH guest
(same checkpoint-restored root, fresh identity) reconciles a lost
fs.write by READ-BACK: already-applied → NOT re-executed; absent →
re-executed exactly once and verified; divergent bytes → Unresolved
(checkpoint restore required). proc.exec is never reconciled (a re-run
is a duplicate external effect) — typed refusal steers to restore.

